# 0010: Backports from the v620/vllm-src fork (v0.24.0-based gfx1030 optimization
# work) onto the 0.27.1 recipe tree. Re-ported by hand - files diverged heavily,
# do NOT expect this to apply to any other vLLM version.
#
# Contents (ranked by measured impact, TP=4 Qwen3.8-27B GPTQ-int4 on 4x V620):
#   1. Triton do_not_specialize on the hot per-step kernels:
#      packed_decode_kernel (FLA fused_recurrent), layer_norm_fwd_kernel
#      (layernorm_guard), _causal_conv1d_update_kernel, fused_gdn_gating_kernel,
#      kernel_unified_attention + reduce_segments (triton_unified_attention),
#      _fused_qk_rmsnorm_rope_gate_kernel. Kills ~20 redundant JIT
#      specialization checks per launch (~600 launches/step at decode).
#   2. models/qwen3_next.py: enable the fused qk-norm+rope+gate kernel on ROCm
#      (is_cuda() -> is_cuda_alike()).
#
#      Item 3 (persistent core_attn_out buffer) was dropped before merging:
#      the zero-fill is load-bearing under CUDA graphs when the batch is
#      padded (the core op writes only the unpadded rows) and the buffer
#      reallocs whenever num_tokens changes, leaving captured graphs with
#      stale addresses. See https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/28182.
#
# Measured (all_reduce PHB-class P2P, MTP=2, BATCHTOK=2048): +3-4% aggregate
# decode across solo short / solo long / 2x-long-concurrent, from
# do_not_specialize alone.
# Applies AFTER patches 0001-0009. Only 0002 overlaps a file
# (vllm/v1/attention/ops/triton_unified_attention.py); this patch expects
# 0002 already applied.
